    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 261 tests pass, including the new `AcceptanceTest`. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `checkDigit` field: a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the owner's `customerCode`, surfaced at read time on `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `checkDigit` property to the Owner response schema (integer 0\u20139, `readOnly`), placed right after `customerCode`. This regenerates `OwnerDto` with a `checkDigit` field on build.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping(target = \"checkDigit\", expression = \"java(checkDigit(owner))\")` and a `checkDigit(Owner)` helper that runs the standard Luhn algorithm over the digit characters of `customerCode` (skipping the hyphens in `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`), returning `null` when the owner or code is absent.\n\nThe mapper's Luhn logic mirrors the test's reference `luhn(...)` implementation exactly (right-to-left, double every second digit starting from the rightmost, subtract 9 when >9, then `(10 - sum%10) % 10`), so the recomputed check digit in the acceptance test matches the returned value.",
